  "notes": "HABS 2011 text sheet: the Solbeck House (Porter IN, 1920s), 'a prime example of the vernacular summer beach cottages built in the Indiana Dunes': one room at first, a balloon frame with exposed studs and a Dutch-lap clapboard exterior with exposed eaves; casements; a front porch overlooking the dunes; sanitation by outhouse and hand pump; reached by a footpath over a dune"
